1
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:32,841
{\an8}THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

2
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:33,801
{\an8}MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

3
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:37,012
{\an8}Has Yue made good progress
in his journey west, I wonder?

4
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:40,182
He stopped to inspect
the papermakers' village,

5
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:42,476
so I predict he's halfway there.

6
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:44,938
Only halfway there, I see.

7
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:51,902
<i>In the absence of Jinshi the eunuch,</i>

8
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:54,239
<i>I'm back to serving the Emperor again.</i>

9
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:58,659
<i>For generations, the Ma clan</i>

10
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,329
<i>has shouldered a duty
to protect the nation's flowers.</i>

11
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:05,375
<i>Therefore, I've known
His Majesty since childhood.</i>

12
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:11,297
<i>The Emperor,
his wet nurse's daughter Ah-Duo...</i>

13
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:14,801
<i>and one other...</i>

14
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:37,740
<i>On their westward journey...</i>

15
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:41,202
<i>Basen is escorting
a flower known as "the Moon."</i>

16
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:43,829
<i>However, Basen once failed</i>

17
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:48,334
<i>and let the Moon get chipped
during his battle against the Shi clan.</i>

18
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:51,295
<i>Although I cannot deny my concern,</i>

19
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:54,464
<i>the apothecary girl's presence
should keep things orderly.</i>

20
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:57,302
<i>I wholeheartedly trust
her mental toughness.</i>

21
00:02:57,927 --> 00:02:58,845
<i>The problem is...</i>

22
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:04,516
<i>why they're visiting the Western Capital
upon departing the papermakers' village.</i>

23
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:09,814
<i>I persuaded my reluctant son
to bring the girl as a food taster.</i>

24
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:13,275
<i>The Moon Prince approved instantly.</i>

25
00:03:13,276 --> 00:03:15,485
A tough road awaits him too.

26
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:17,946
What sort of flowers shall flock his way?

27
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:21,158
Flocking flowers, sir?
Quite the amusing choice of words.

28
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:24,328
Likening them to insects
would be offensive, you see.

29
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:27,039
You'd understand
after seeing my flower garden.

30
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,417
<i>An air of loneliness shrouds His Majesty.</i>

31
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:34,047
<i>Perhaps because Ah-Duo,
the head of this villa, is absent.</i>

32
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:36,966
<i>She's headed
for the Western Capital as well.</i>

33
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:39,427
<i>Alongside a certain someone...</i>

34
00:03:41,721 --> 00:03:43,056
Locust plague, huh?

35
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,307
<i>Locust plagues.</i>

36
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:48,144
<i>In many cases,
they swarm in from the West.</i>

37
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:52,731
<i>The Moon Prince has been tasked with
devising countermeasures.</i>

38
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:55,234
<i>With grasshoppers coming from the West,</i>

39
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:57,904
<i>they've probably caused damage there, too.</i>

40
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:00,322
<i>Starvation makes people unruly.</i>

41
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:03,910
<i>This has sparked wars
many times in the past.</i>

42
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:07,537
{\an8}Hopefully, it's an unnecessary concern.

43
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:08,705
Yes.

44
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:12,709
<i>The Yi clan, previous rulers
of Isei-shu in the West...</i>

45
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:13,627
YI CLAN

46
00:04:13,628 --> 00:04:15,004
<i>...died out over a decade ago.</i>

47
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:19,425
<i>During the Empress Regnant's reign,
they were destroyed after plotting evil.</i>

48
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:24,973
<i>Governing the area now
is Empress Gyokuyou's father, Gyokuen.</i>

49
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:30,186
<i>They're nameless now, but His Majesty
should eventually grant them a name.</i>

50
00:04:31,062 --> 00:04:34,816
<i>If a war breaks out,
the West shall become pivotal.</i>

51
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:38,819
<i>That's why Empress Gyokuyou
was taken as the official wife.</i>

52
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:41,947
<i>Marriage is yet another political tool.</i>

53
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:44,074
Even from the throne of a nation,

54
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:46,953
one must occasionally flatter
their father-in-law, eh?

55
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:51,666
Sometimes, I must make
my own hardships known as well.

56
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:08,975
<i>The federal state of Hokuaren
lies northwest of the Country of Li.</i>

57
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:14,104
<i>This vast grain-producing region,
rich in woodland resources,</i>

58
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,065
<i>has a history
of frequent conflict with Li.</i>

59
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:20,652
As for why barbarian tribes
currently pester the Country of Li,

60
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:23,448
the cause lies within Hokuaren.

61
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:27,784
With no diplomatic relations,
we can't communicate directly.

62
00:05:27,785 --> 00:05:30,037
So, by having other countries mediate...

63
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:31,956
Wait, are you even listening?

64
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:33,499
I'm listening.

65
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:38,086
Foreign officials gather
in the Western Capital we're headed to.

66
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:41,215
People with ties to Hokuaren
are coming too, you know.

67
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:44,134
<i>The Western Capital came as a shock.</i>

68
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:47,804
<i>Even by wagon and boat,
this'll take over half a month.</i>

69
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:51,558
<i>I wonder if Chou-u and Sazen
will be okay without me.</i>

70
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:53,352
<i>I guess they'll manage somehow.</i>

71
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:57,689
<i>So that's why Sir Basen is nagging me</i>

72
00:05:57,690 --> 00:06:00,276
<i>with a crash course
in annoying political affairs.</i>

73
00:06:03,696 --> 00:06:04,781
We're almost there.

74
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:08,909
Ouch.

75
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,536
We'll spend the night in this village.

76
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:12,497
Don't wander off.

77
00:06:14,874 --> 00:06:16,374
I'll go buy food.

78
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:18,252
Do you hear me when I speak?

79
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:21,463
Sir Ji--

80
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:22,715
I'll go with you.

81
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:24,717
<i>This guy...</i>

82
00:06:28,679 --> 00:06:30,681
Are they selling anything amusing?

83
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:32,849
Something amusing...

84
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:36,311
Hemp seems to be
a thriving crop around here.

85
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:38,105
Their clothing is mostly hemp.

86
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:42,527
Since that's probably not warm enough,
they combine it with animal fur.

87
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:49,241
Even the bread is topped with hemp seeds,
and it looks like they're using oil.

88
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:50,909
Frying in oil?

89
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:52,577
And then there's...

90
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:53,538
What?

91
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:55,872
Never mind.

92
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:58,251
I suspect they're smoking too much.

93
00:06:58,793 --> 00:06:59,960
Smoking too much?

94
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:03,588
In small portions,
hemp is used for medicine.

95
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:06,383
But routine smoking can be addictive.

96
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:08,886
In large amounts, it's also poisonous.

97
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:12,431
I thought you were obsessed with
anything poisonous.

98
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:15,559
Addictive substances are scary, you know.

99
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,395
You can't get rid of poison
whenever you want.

100
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:19,980
Even if you try quitting,

101
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:23,526
the temptation is greater
than warm bedding on a winter morning.

102
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:25,318
Really?

103
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:28,405
If your room is warm,
getting out of bed is easy.

104
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:32,076
<i>Dang it, this guy
can't even fathom plebeian values.</i>

105
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:34,828
<i>Before Sir Jinshi wakes up,</i>

106
00:07:34,829 --> 00:07:38,332
<i>I'm sure the old gal fires up
a charcoal heater to warm up his room.</i>

107
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:43,170
<i>Overworking the elderly Ms. Suiren?
What a cruel master.</i>

108
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:46,549
<i>He doesn't even seem to realize
how strenuous that is.</i>

109
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:50,302
{\an8}I haven't seen those eyes in a while.

110
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:52,555
<i>Is this guy sane?</i>

111
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:55,433
More importantly, let's buy food.

112
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:57,434
What's this?

113
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:58,977
A snack called <i>mahua.</i>

114
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:01,314
They twist the dough and deep-fry it.

115
00:08:02,398 --> 00:08:05,066
<i>Would aristocrats fancy this, I wonder?</i>

116
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:06,776
One, please.

117
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:07,653
Comin' up.

118
00:08:08,404 --> 00:08:11,072
One's not enough. How about another?

119
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:12,617
Sure, if it's good.

120
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:15,953
Come on, you're hogging it?

121
00:08:17,246 --> 00:08:18,122
Checking for poison.

122
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:22,209
<i>It's freshly fried, which helps.</i>

123
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,253
<i>I think everyone would eat this.</i>

124
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:26,254
I'd like a whole bunch.

125
00:08:26,255 --> 00:08:27,089
Coming right up.

126
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:32,594
Not bad.

127
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:35,931
<i>I mean, if this flavor
beats your usual court meals,</i>

128
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:38,308
<i>your chefs should probably quit.</i>

129
00:08:38,309 --> 00:08:41,394
Sir Jinshi, are you sure
you should be goofing off?

130
00:08:41,395 --> 00:08:45,023
Basen seems worn out
from that papermakers' village.

131
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:48,110
Me slacking off for a bit
will do wonders for him too.

132
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:50,362
I see.

133
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:53,698
<i>Sir Basen certainly seems
terrible at lying.</i>

134
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:57,160
<i>Playing Sir Jinshi's boss
must've been a lot to endure.</i>

135
00:08:57,161 --> 00:09:01,040
<i>He takes after Sir Gaoshun,
getting tummy aches over stuff like that.</i>

136
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:04,918
Okay, let's get back to gathering food.

137
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,087
Agreed.

138
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:11,509
Is this...

139
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:14,177
Excuse me.

140
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:15,220
Can I help you?

141
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:17,430
Could you share some with us?

142
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:19,141
We'll pay for it.

143
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:25,230
Which would you like?

144
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:27,857
This, this, and that. About ten portions.

145
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:30,485
And something amusing, if you have it.

146
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:32,238
Sit tight for a bit.

147
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:34,322
<i>Oh?</i>

148
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:37,158
<i>She's giving us the good stuff.</i>

149
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,703
As for the price...

150
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,996
how about this much?

151
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,915
<i>Cheaper than I thought.</i>

152
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,918
Sorry for asking you to do all this.

153
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:51,506
Well, you never know
when the gods could be watching.

154
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:53,843
See? There's one right here.

155
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:59,639
I see you worship snakes here.

156
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,141
Yeah, we do.

157
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:04,228
White snakes bring
abundant harvests for the year.

158
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:10,234
<i>I'm sure Sir Jinshi has heard about
the White Lady by now.</i>

159
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:14,238
<i>He might even be
in charge of countermeasures.</i>

160
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:19,451
<i>Where could she have gone?
That suspicious immortal maiden...</i>

161
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:23,538
If you folks are headed west,
you'd better be careful.

162
00:10:23,539 --> 00:10:24,914
Why's that?

163
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:29,252
Those main roads in the West
are crawling with thieves lately.

164
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:31,421
Even the merchants avoid them.

165
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:32,839
<i>Now I get it.</i>

166
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:36,676
<i>Maybe she used to sell the food
on these shelves to those merchants.</i>

167
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,095
<i>That's why I got them cheap.</i>

168
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,930
Thank you. We'll be careful.

169
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:43,351
Here you go. Take care.

170
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:51,399
Shall we head back soon?

171
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,444
Yeah, let's go.

172
00:11:02,286 --> 00:11:04,288
Pardon me. We're back.

173
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:07,791
Did you ready the horses?

174
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:10,543
Yes sir.
They'll be ready tomorrow morning.

175
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:13,296
But they come with
a packhorse hauler as a guide.

176
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:16,300
Guide? So it's a cargo carrier
using packhorses?

177
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,012
Tea, now!

178
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:24,015
I'll fetch some hot water.

179
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:25,600
No, you're fine.

180
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:26,644
I like it lukewarm.

181
00:11:30,689 --> 00:11:32,565
I heard about the thieves.

182
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:34,360
Right, I was told as well.

183
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:37,654
A kind that charges so-called "tolls."

184
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:41,825
Upon encountering them,
if our guide can talk us out of it,

185
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:44,536
they'll let us go
for a chunk of our cargo.

186
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:49,082
That's why they won't lend us horses
unless we hire a guide?

187
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:49,917
Yes sir.

188
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:53,711
<i>Both of them are trained warriors.</i>

189
00:11:53,712 --> 00:11:56,881
<i>Although their positions
wouldn't normally tolerate thieves,</i>

190
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:58,634
<i>they don't have time to fight.</i>

191
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:05,391
<i>I just hope we don't bump into any.</i>

192
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:16,610
Wow, that really happened?

193
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:18,903
Tell me more, Lady Ah-Duo.

194
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:21,698
Things about your past that I don't know.

195
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:23,575
Sure, of course,

196
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:25,869
but let's take a break first.

197
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:28,371
Aren't you tired from chatting so much?

198
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:30,331
I'm just fine.

199
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:33,751
I never get to spend
this much time with you.

200
00:12:33,752 --> 00:12:36,337
I could talk all day long.

201
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:40,091
We have plenty of time.
There's still a long road ahead.

202
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:41,217
But...

203
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:44,722
Besides, travel fatigue
always creeps up on you.

204
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:47,891
It's important to rest whenever you can.

205
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:49,018
Yes ma'am.

206
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:53,564
In that case, Lady Ah-Duo,
can we do it just like before?

207
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:10,455
<i>Just like before, huh?</i>

208
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:12,625
<i>How long ago was that, again?</i>

209
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:22,008
Come on, now.

210
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:23,928
What, you've had enough already?

211
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,640
Shut up. I know what I'm doing.

212
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:30,934
Then return to your ladies-in-waiting.

213
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:32,478
They're in tears.

214
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:35,523
You have an important duty. Get it done.

215
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:40,569
We're only a year apart.
Don't treat me like a kid!

216
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,113
Good point.

217
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:46,116
Didn't you eat off that?

218
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,536
You don't have to eat it.

219
00:14:00,589 --> 00:14:03,800
At the very least,
I want to choose my own companion.

220
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:05,218
Don't be ridiculous.

221
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:08,930
You're given everything
in the highest quality possible.

222
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:11,767
You can't partake in anything inferior.

223
00:14:12,434 --> 00:14:15,813
If you did that,
tons of people would suffer.

224
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:18,065
They were older than Mother.

225
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:22,069
Come on, don't say things
that are hard to respond to.

226
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:24,113
I know, but...

227
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:26,573
Be an adult.

228
00:14:26,574 --> 00:14:28,157
Easy for you to say.

229
00:14:28,158 --> 00:14:31,203
In my shoes, do you think
you could accept this calmly?

230
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:32,830
Well, then...

231
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:39,336
{\an8}I've decided.

232
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:40,921
Decided what?

233
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,760
My companion for tonight.

234
00:14:47,344 --> 00:14:48,220
What?

235
00:14:56,729 --> 00:15:01,400
<i>Even after that, I never thought
he'd make me an Eastern Palace concubine.</i>

236
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:21,128
<i>I saw the boy occasionally
and watched him grow up.</i>

237
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:22,796
<i>In addition...</i>

238
00:15:27,676 --> 00:15:32,264
<i>I also protected a young Concubine Lishu
from the previous emperor.</i>

239
00:15:37,436 --> 00:15:38,353
What happened?

240
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:40,730
- Lady Ah-Duo...
- It's the thieves!

241
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:42,149
What?

242
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,238
<i>Will we reach the mountains soon?</i>

243
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:53,493
If thieves appear, it'll be around here.

244
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:56,579
A passage between two mountains.

245
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,498
Perfect to attack from both sides.

246
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:02,460
They're not dumb either,
so it's best that nobody dies.

247
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:05,881
They'll let us off the hook
if we leave half of our cargo.

248
00:16:07,257 --> 00:16:10,969
And we only encounter them
about a third of the time, so...

249
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,595
<i>I see.</i>

250
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:16,099
<i>That's a frequency
the merchants would consider.</i>

251
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,267
<i>They don't get attacked every time,</i>

252
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:20,478
<i>and taking detours
would raise labor costs.</i>

253
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:23,773
You can just think of it
as a slightly expensive toll.

254
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:26,734
They call themselves
"thieves of justice," you know.

255
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:27,861
Thieves of justice?

256
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:33,283
<i>If thieves actually attack us,
can this guy "stay" like a good dog?</i>

257
00:16:37,788 --> 00:16:41,457
<i>Sir Jinshi seems to have
taken a liking to desert horses.</i>

258
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:43,544
<i>He left the wagon to ride horseback.</i>

259
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:46,547
<i>Therefore, Sir Basen's riding a horse too.</i>

260
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:51,010
<i>Which means I get
this spacious wagon all to myself.</i>

261
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:54,470
<i>Sitting for too long makes my butt hurt.</i>

262
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:56,640
<i>So, I think I'll lie down.</i>

263
00:16:57,474 --> 00:17:01,353
Thieves may not even come,
so there's no point in worrying.

264
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:03,397
Time for a nap.

265
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:17,076
What was that?

266
00:17:17,077 --> 00:17:19,704
Well, it looks like thieves appeared

267
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:22,708
and attacked another wagon
passing through before us.

268
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:25,418
It's best to wait this out.

269
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:27,253
<i>Basically, if we wait here,</i>

270
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:29,798
<i>we'll get through unscathed?</i>

271
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:33,969
{\an8}Hang on?

272
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:36,929
Heading out!

273
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:37,931
Yes, sir!

274
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:43,853
I see you took a nap.

275
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:45,271
Whatever do you mean?

276
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:47,441
There's a strange mark on your cheek.

277
00:17:50,027 --> 00:17:52,154
Anyway, what happened here?

278
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:56,032
This design...

279
00:17:56,033 --> 00:17:56,867
Yeah.

280
00:17:57,534 --> 00:18:00,536
Ah-Duo's wagon was attacked.

281
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:03,206
What is Lady Ah-Duo doing here?

282
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:08,211
<i>But I'm sure Lady Ah-Duo could've talked
them into just taking their valuables.</i>

283
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:10,089
Concubine Lishu is with her.

284
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:11,589
What?

285
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:14,217
<i>For some reason,
my anxiety is skyrocketing.</i>

286
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:16,636
<i>That concubine is oddly prone to disaster.</i>

287
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:20,181
Will they be all right with so few guards?

288
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:23,102
If anything, Basen alone should be enough.

289
00:18:41,912 --> 00:18:45,582
<i>How much of a fight did they put up
to end up with so many broken bones?</i>

290
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:49,795
<i>What's that?</i>

291
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:51,421
What in the world...

292
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:55,384
You said money would appease them!

293
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:59,345
I was prepared to offer them our cargo,

294
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,306
but they wanted to sell the girl.

295
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:04,892
She's under my care,
so I couldn't let that happen.

296
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:08,229
Oh, no. This must be some mistake.

297
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,482
I have no idea
how things ended up like this...

298
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:20,325
Pardon me.

299
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,078
<i>The severed end was crushed.</i>

300
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:28,541
<i>Had it come off more cleanly,
my old man could've reattached it.</i>

301
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,543
<i>But I don't have that skill set.</i>

302
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:33,505
<i>If we force it back on,
the arm will just rot and fall off.</i>

303
00:19:34,047 --> 00:19:35,465
<i>I'll do what I can for now.</i>

304
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:43,015
Use this.

305
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:46,435
It took a while
treating the injuries over there.

306
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:48,937
You came with them too?

307
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:53,483
Yes, I had my doubts
about being allowed to leave that palace.

308
00:19:54,234 --> 00:19:56,235
<i>She's here too.</i>

309
00:19:56,236 --> 00:19:58,822
<i>What's happening in the Western Capital?</i>

310
00:20:01,325 --> 00:20:02,783
Are you good at stitching?

311
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:04,702
Only the basics.

312
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:07,206
I'm sorry there's no anesthetic, though.

313
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,627
Power through the pain.

314
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:28,644
<i>Apparently, the robbery
was a miscalculation of sorts.</i>

315
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:34,774
<i>They were posing as the entourage
of a rich boy sent to a provincial post,</i>

316
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:37,777
<i>but the thieves apparently realized
how important they were.</i>

317
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:40,030
<i>Well, with this bunch,
what can you expect?</i>

318
00:20:44,409 --> 00:20:45,826
If I may.

319
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:47,746
Yes, come in.

320
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:52,209
I was instructed
to speak with you directly.

321
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,880
<i>Why is Lady Lishu even here?</i>

322
00:20:57,881 --> 00:21:00,842
<i>Concubines shouldn't be allowed
to leave the rear palace.</i>

323
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:04,345
<i>Not to mention Suirei.</i>

324
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:06,013
<i>Given her talent,</i>

325
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:09,184
<i>I see why they'd bring her on trips
as a makeshift doctor.</i>

326
00:21:09,893 --> 00:21:12,938
<i>Even so,
it's definitely a bit problematic.</i>

327
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,732
"What's a concubine doing here?"

328
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:18,276
That's your question, right?

329
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:19,694
Yes ma'am.

330
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:22,948
Have you heard the reason
Basen is heading to the West?

331
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:28,703
<i>Because Sir Jinshi is in disguise,
she's using Basen's name to play along.</i>

332
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:31,080
<i>Lady Ah-Duo, thoughtful as always.</i>

333
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:33,166
A gathering in the West, I heard.

334
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:37,045
With Sir Basen attending
alongside other government authorities.

335
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,548
We'll be attending as well.

336
00:21:40,048 --> 00:21:42,091
With a concubine riding along,

337
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:44,510
we avoided traveling in a large group.

338
00:21:44,511 --> 00:21:48,932
Or rather, we were treated as a nuisance.

339
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:51,934
<i>She's hinting at something.</i>

340
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:56,565
<i>I can't imagine why they need Lady Lishu
at some gathering in the West.</i>

341
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:59,525
<i>If it was Empress Gyokuyou,
who's from the West,</i>

342
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:02,529
<i>or Concubine Lihua, who's related
to the Emperor, I would get it.</i>

343
00:22:05,615 --> 00:22:09,244
After all,
this is also about choosing a wife.

344
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:11,704
A wife?

345
00:22:11,705 --> 00:22:12,913
Yes.

346
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:14,916
For the imperial younger brother.

347
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:48,885
PREVIEW OF THE NEXT EPISODE

348
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:58,144
{\an8}<i>The next episode is,
"Problems Accumulate."</i>

349
00:23:58,145 --> 00:24:00,939
{\an8}Subtitle translation by: Logan Lampkins

